ue,"url":"https://councilmeetings.lewisham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Mayor and Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://councilmeetings.lewisham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Governance Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://councilmeetings.lewisham.gov.uk"}]},"news":[{"title":"Green-led council plans to ban cooperation with Home Office on immigration raids","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/jul/15/green-led-council-plans-to-ban-cooperation-with-home-office-on-immigration-raids","source":"Guardian local government","published":"Wed, 15 Jul 2026 05:00:46 GMT","severity":"low","summary":"<p>Exclusive: Lewisham council\u2019s move marks first step in Greens\u2019 plan to create a corridor of sanctuary boroughs across London</p><p>A Green-led London council is planning to ban its officials from working with the Home Office on immigration raids, after uncovering evidence suggesting government officials wanted to use environmental health data to target restaurant workers.</p><p>Councillors on the Lewisham borough council are due to vote next week on a motion that would review its systems with a view to ending any cooperation with the government\u2019s attempts to deport people without the right ","paywalled":false}],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Building for Lewisham Strategic Partner scheme commits \u00a395.8m while completing procurement","lead":"This represents 12% of the full capital programme committed dependent on completing a procurement. Given the historical slippage on this programme, delivery and funding risk are material for lenders.","iso":"2026-07-22","paper_title":"Capital Programme Budget","paper_url":"https://lewisham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s152132/152132.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Contingent \u00a3775.73m GLA housing grant bid, with \u00a350.99m additional borrowing if approved","lead":"This massive contingent commitment creates material forecast uncertainty. If the bid succeeds, borrowing increases significantly; if it fails, housing delivery targets may be missed. Lenders need clarity on which scenario is planned for.","iso":"2026-07-22","paper_title":"Capital Programme Budget","paper_url":"https://lewisham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s152132/152132.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"\u00a310m contingency funded from reserves for urgent risks and pressures","lead":"Reserve-funded contingencies indicate either incomplete budgeting for known risks or identified-but-unquantified pressures. Drawing reserves to fund contingencies indicates pressure on the council's financial cushion.","iso":"2026-07-22","paper_title":"Capital Programme Budget","paper_url":"https://lewisham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s152132/152132.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Capital Programme Budget","paper_url":"https://lewisham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s152132/152132.pdf","headline":"Building for Lewisham Strategic Partner scheme commits \u00a395.8m while completing procurement","detail":"The council has included \u00a395.8m for the first schemes (Thomas Lane Yard and Achilles regeneration phases 1-2) dependent on completing a Strategic Partner procurement. This major scheme experienced \u00a311.4m slippage in the previous year.","category":"capital","matters":"This represents 12% of the full capital programme committed dependent on completing a procurement. Given the historical slippage on this programme, delivery and funding risk are material for lenders.","figures":"\u00a395.8m budget for first schemes; prior year BfL slippage \u00a311.4m (55% of budget)","quote":"A key delivery mechanism is the conclusion of the procurement of a Strategic Partner. This has resulted in the inclusion of the programme and the \u00a395.8m budget needed for the first schemes.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Capital Programme Budget","paper_url":"https://lewisham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s152132/152132.pdf","headline":"Contingent \u00a3775.73m GLA housing grant bid, with \u00a350.99m additional borrowing if approved","detail":"The council has bid for \u00a3775.73m of affordable housing grant from the GLA to deliver 3,070 homes over 10 years. If successful, this would increase the capital programme by \u00a3169.5m over four years and trigger \u00a350.99m additional borrowing. The bid outcome is not yet known and any approval will require Mayor and Cabinet decision.","category":"capital","matters":"This massive contingent commitment creates material forecast uncertainty. If the bid succeeds, borrowing increases significantly; if it fails, housing delivery targets may be missed. Lenders need clarity on which scenario is planned for.","figures":"\u00a3775.73m grant bid pending; potential programme increase \u00a3169,516,311 over four years; potential additional borrowing \u00a350,991,293","quote":"The Council has put forward an ambitious bid to the GLA for \u00a3775.73m of affordable housing grant to deliver 3,070 homes over for the next 10 years. Whilst we are yet to hear the outcome from this... if successful this could increase the programme over the next four years by \u00a3169,516,311","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Capital Programme Budget","paper_url":"https://lewisham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s152132/152132.pdf","headline":"\u00a310m contingency funded from reserves for urgent risks and pressures","detail":"The council has included a \u00a310m contingency budget (split between HRA and general fund) funded from reserves to cover urgent works that preclude formal member approval in advance. Use of this contingency will draw down reserves and be reported to members retrospectively.","category":"reserves","matters":"Reserve-funded contingencies indicate either incomplete budgeting for known risks or identified-but-unquantified pressures. Drawing reserves to fund contingencies indicates pressure on the council's financial cushion.","figures":"\u00a310m contingency budget across HRA and general fund, funded from reserves","quote":"The inclusion of a \u00a310m contingency budget into the 2026/27 budget... will ensure that works of an urgent nature can be delivered. The \u00a310m, if needed, will be funded from reserves in 2026/27","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Capital Programme Budget","paper_url":"https://lewisham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s152132/152132.pdf","headline":"\u00a3293.2m of external borrowing committed across the expanded capital programme","detail":"The council is committing \u00a3293.2m of prudential borrowing to deliver the current capital programme: \u00a351.5m from the general fund and \u00a3241.7m from the HRA. The council states this remains within Treasury Management Strategy tolerances, but represents material debt commitment.","category":"borrowing","matters":"High borrowing levels constrain future financial flexibility and increase debt servicing costs. Lenders need to assess whether debt levels are sustainable and whether there is headroom for additional borrowing if external funding sources fail.","figures":"\u00a3293.2m total external borrowing (\u00a351.5m general fund; \u00a3241.7m HRA)","quote":"The agreed budget forecast \u00a3293.2m of external borrowing to deliver the current programme, meaning that the decisions within this report would not breach the agreed Treasury Management Strategy (TMS)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Capital Programme Budget","paper_url":"https://lewisham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s152132/152132.pdf","headline":"Capital programme increased by \u00a3231.1m (43%) in a single update cycle","detail":"The approved capital programme was expanded from \u00a3539.3m (March 2026 budget) to \u00a3770.3m, a net increase of \u00a3231.1m. This includes \u00a395.8m for the Building for Lewisham Strategic Partner schemes and \u00a368m added to future HRA years to align with the 30-year business plan.","category":"capital","matters":"A 43% programme expansion in a single update signals either incomplete original planning or significant replanning between March and July. For lenders, this raises questions about forecast accuracy and financial control.","figures":"\u00a328.3m increase for 2026/27; \u00a3202.7m increase for 2027/28 onward; total net increase \u00a3231.1m","quote":"Agree that the cumulative impact of all the above recommendations is a net increase of \u00a328.3m for 2026/27 and an increase of \u00a3202.7m for 2027/28 onward, totalling a net increase to the full Capital Programme of \u00a3231.1m.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-22"},"name":"Lewisham","findings_total":122,"news_drafts_total":3}}